Subject: search /run, mask implicit basenames, and fix settings path parsing
Source: downstream patch for Vulkan-Loader vulkan-sdk-1.4.328.1
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on adding a /run tier, merging the
default driver/layer/settings search by basename, and the
check_if_settings_path_exists() segment-parsing fix

read_data_files_in_search_paths() built the default driver and layer search
path from the user and XDG directories, the additive VK_ADD_DRIVER_FILES /
VK_ADD_LAYER_PATH entries, then SYSCONFDIR (compiled as /etc) and the XDG
data directories (falling back to /usr/local/share and /usr/share). It never
searched /run. add_data_files() then opened every JSON file in every
directory named by that search path with no basename deduplication at all,
so a driver or layer manifest installed under both /etc/vulkan/icd.d and
/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d with the same basename loaded twice instead of the
higher tier replacing the lower one; duplicate directory removal in
read_data_files_in_search_paths only drops repeated directory strings, it
never shadows a same-named file across distinct directories. Separately,
get_unix_settings_path() selected the single vk_loader_settings.json by
trying the user and XDG paths, then SYSCONFDIR, then the XDG data
directories, also with no /run tier, and check_if_settings_path_exists()'s
own colon-splitting parser had a pre-existing off-by-one: after finding the
first PATH_SEPARATOR in a multi-entry base string, it resumed the next
segment at the separator's own index instead of one past it, so every
segment after the first was checked with a leading stray separator
character glued onto its front and could never match a real path. With the
ordinary two-entry XDG_DATA_DIRS fallback of "/usr/local/share:/usr/share",
that bug made the second, real vendor entry ("/usr/share") permanently
unreachable.

Add a compiled-in NEX_RUNSTATEDIR of "/run" and search it between SYSCONFDIR
and the XDG data directories in both readers, so the default driver, layer,
and settings search covers /etc, then /run, then /usr/share, after the
unchanged upstream user and XDG priority.

Fix check_if_settings_path_exists() to advance to stop + 1 (one past the
separator) when starting the next segment, and to skip a zero-length
segment produced by a leading, trailing, or repeated separator, instead of
folding the separator into the next segment's path. This is a correctness
fix to the reader this patch is repairing, not a separate change: every
multi-entry base string this function walks, including the ordinary
XDG_DATA_DIRS fallback, was affected.

Give add_data_files() a new mask_duplicate_basenames parameter. When set,
a file is skipped if a file with the same basename is already present in
out_files, checked by scanning out_files itself rather than a separate
allocated table, so there is no extra allocation that can fail
independently of out_files's own allocation (which add_if_manifest_file
already reports through the ordinary VkResult error path). A directory
read (readdir) failure while masking is active fails the whole search
(VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED) instead of risking an unmasked
lower-priority duplicate from a directory whose remaining entries were
never seen.

read_data_files_in_search_paths() now builds an additional, independent
additive_search_path buffer on COMMON_UNIX_PLATFORMS when no override is
active, holding only VK_ADD_DRIVER_FILES / VK_ADD_LAYER_PATH. It is always
searched first and with mask_duplicate_basenames=false, so two additive
entries that share a basename both load, preserving every duplicate exactly
as upstream did; because both land in out_files first, either one still
masks a same-named file from the implicit tiers scanned next in search_path.
search_path itself is searched with a new mask_search_path flag, which the
COMMON_UNIX_PLATFORMS branch sets to true exactly when there is no override
path active, giving the compiled-in tiers Nex's basename-shadowing priority.

This additive/implicit split, and the masking it enables, applies only to
COMMON_UNIX_PLATFORMS. read_data_files_in_search_paths() never gave Windows
an implicit system tier to mask against in the first place -- the registry
search that supplies Windows's driver and layer manifests happens separately,
in loader_windows.c -- so the _WIN32 branch is left exactly as upstream had
it: additional_env and package_path share one single search_path buffer,
sized and copied together with no split, no additive_search_path, and
mask_search_path staying false. loader_windows.c's own registry-backed
add_data_files call also keeps mask_duplicate_basenames as false. An explicit
override list -- VK_DRIVER_FILES, VK_ICD_FILENAMES, VK_LAYER_PATH, or a
caller-supplied override -- still builds and searches a single unmasked
search_path exactly as upstream did, on every platform, with no additive
buffer at all.

